OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775044735
OL,1,Vk4                               G4/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKURDS FLEE AS IRAQI TROOPS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTAKE KEY CITIES
OL,5, Thousands of Kurdish civilians are
OL,6, fleeing to Iraq's northern mountains as
OL,7, Iraqi troops continue to advance.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FGovernment troops have retaken the key
OL,10,Fnorthern cities of Dohuk and Erbil from
OL,11,FKurdish guerrillas and, reportedly, the
OL,12,Fonly border crossing with Turkey.
OL,14,FThe US has not responded to requests by
OL,15,Frebels to shoot down Iraqi helicopter
OL,16,Fgunships being used against them.
OL,18,FMeanwhile, rebels have denied claims
OL,19,Fthat Iraqi government troops have
OL,20,Frecaptured the strategic town of Zakho
OL,21,F- Iraq's most northern Kurdish town.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG01-04-91F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1775044735
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/27
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGSADDAM'S TROOPS "CONTROL
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGSOUTH-WESTERN IRAQ"
OL,4,D
OL,5, Reports coming out of southern Iraq say
OL,6, government troops are now in control of
OL,7, the south-west of the country.
OL,9,FRefugees from the area say the city of
OL,10,FSamawah, held by Shi'ite Muslim rebels,
OL,11,Fhas now fallen to the Iraqi army.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FA BBC correspondent says the fall of
OL,14,FSamawah brings to an end rebel hopes
OL,15,Ffor an organised revolt in the south.
OL,17,FMeanwhile, Western journalists taken on
OL,18,Fa tour of the northern oil city of
OL,19,FKirkuk say they found it was firmly in
OL,20,Fthe hands of government forces.
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG01-04-91
OL,23,D]F Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
